You totally fail to respond to my points about reduplication of
effort, inefficiency, brand awareness, and the inappropriate ownership
mentality.  Yes, the internet can become filled with teams of people
all over the place running their own nethack improvement projects,
creating ever more branches and spinoffs and patchfiles and confusion.
Why, why that competing-team model??  Nethack, the game, the main game
that many of us would like to see improved, doesn't need copycats and
competition to get the work of improvement done.  It needs a
development process, as I've said before, that is more transparent and
more responsive to user needs.


